{
 "about": "Expected verdicts of `modelspec lint` for every corpus item, under both profiles. An item is a file (hcl/, json/) or a directory (modules/: a SpecScore project in the SpecScore layout; standalone/: files linted together, with `modules` as --module assignments relative to the item). `differs` names the reader whose recorded verdict (testdata/golden) is different, and says why: specscore is compared with the default profile, the Directory's JSON reader with the publish profile. An item under parts/ is one file of another item, given alone (as an editor or a hook would): `path` is where it is under this directory, and a module is the unit, so its verdict is that of the whole module it belongs to. Parts are not compared with the other readers, which lint a whole project. An item without `differs` must have the same verdict as the reader recorded for it.",
 "items": {
  "hcl/blank-property-name.modelspec.hcl": {
   "default": {
    "verdict": "refuse",
    "rules": [
     "name-form"
    ]
   },
   "publish": {
    "verdict": "refuse",
    "rules": [
     "name-form",
     "publish-name-form"
    ]
   },
   "differs": {
    "specscore": "specscore accepts a property named by a blank string; no property of that name could ever be referenced, so the standard cannot mean it to be valid (spec/core-model.md: names identify)"
   }
  },
